|---|-----------|------|------|----------|
| R1 | Claim disposition (AC1) | Tests show refusals naming `claims[i].disposition` for a missing and an unknown value, `claims[i].sweep` for a `fixed` claim without one and a `disputed` claim with one, an unknown claim key refused, no reviewer launched and no result recorded for a refusal, and a valid `disputed` claim accepted | Any Pass condition is unmet or untested | `cli/test/sweep-records.test.js` |
| R2 | Sweep record (AC2) | Tests show each of the six fields refused by path when missing, each text field refused when empty, when not text and when over the bound, `sites` refused when not a list, `sites` refused when empty, over 256, or with a bad `path` or `line` (by path), an unknown sweep or site key refused, and a one-site record accepted | Any Pass condition is unmet or untested | `cli/test/sweep-records.test.js` |
| R3 | Records reach later rounds (AC3) | Tests show a paired round's packets carrying the records of its own fixed claims with `classId` and `round`; the next round's packets carrying them without new claims; an individual tagged review carrying them; a dropped claim contributing none; the same record from both peers carried once and a later re-claim of the same finding carried as a second record; no field without records; records not carried after the scope closes; and `roundPolicy.revision` present | Any Pass condition is unmet or untested | `cli/test/sweep-records.test.js` |
| R4 | Regression rule (AC4) | Tests show, at round 4, a new medium finding of a swept class blocks (FAIL), an earlier medium finding of the class still `present` blocks, a medium finding of another class is demoted (PASS), and the claimed finding's own ID is not a class regression | Any Pass condition is unmet or untested | `cli/test/sweep-records.test.js` |
